# SaveVideoKit — public video / audio download & inspect

Use the `savevideokit` MCP server to download or inspect public videos/audio. No API key required.

## Tools
- `inspect_video({url})` → metadata + formats, plus `direct_download_available` and `direct_options[]` (`{download_url, ext, resolution, width, height, filesize}`)
- `create_download({url, format?, quality?})` → `job_id` (only when no direct option exists)
- `get_download_status({job_id})` → `{status, progress, download_url}`; generated files are kept 30 minutes
- `get_supported_sites({})` → service/engine version + verified (32) / featured (33) / all sites (1735)

## Workflow
1. `inspect_video` first, and read the title.
2. **If `direct_options` is non-empty, use it — skip `create_download`.** The URL answers `302` to the original media file on the source CDN, so no server-side download, merge or storage is involved. Save it at once:
   `scripts/download_file.py "<download_url>" "<dir>" --name "<title>" --ext "<option.ext>" --referer "<webpage_url>"`
3. Only when no direct option exists: `create_download({url, format: "mp4"})`, parse `job_id`, poll `get_download_status` every ~5s until `success` / `failed` / `expired`, then save `download_url` with the same script.
4. Always save under the video title (never a random id); the MCP only returns a URL and never writes to disk.
5. Verify the saved file exists and size > 0.

## Limits
- Public content only; no private/age-restricted/region-locked; no watermark removal; no playlists/batch.
- No platform gate: any public URL can be attempted.
- Direct links are signed and expire — on `403`/`404`, re-run `inspect_video` instead of retrying the old URL.
- A job `download_url` expires after ~30 minutes; then create a new `create_download` task.

See `references/constraints.md` for details.

## Keeping up to date

On first activation in a session, check for a newer release and auto-update the SaveVideoKit skill/rule:

```
python3 cursor/scripts/check_update.py --auto
```

This compares `VERSION` with the latest GitHub release of SaveVideoKit/mcp (cached 24h) and updates the `cursor/` folder in place when a newer release exists, keeping a `<dir>.bak-<timestamp>` backup. Use `--check` to only report, `--force` to bypass the cache.
